arm64emu (src/arm64emu)
-----------------------

The AArch64 CPU interpreter, the device models (virtio-mmio, fw_cfg, PSCI,
GICv2, PL011, PL031, virtio-blk/net/console/9p), and the user-mode network
stack are original implementations. They interoperate with the QEMU "virt"
platform, EDK2 firmware, and the Linux kernel by targeting those projects'
public hardware and software interfaces; no third-party source code is
included or distributed with this project.

src/arm64emu/fdt/virt.dts (and its compiled form src/arm64emu/fdt/virt_dtb.h)
is a device-tree blob generated by QEMU for the "virt" machine, with seeds
zeroed for reproducibility. It is functional hardware-description data, not
part of the Apache-licensed source, and carries no separate copyright claim.

arm64chroot (src/arm64chroot)
-----------------------------

arm64chroot is an original implementation (C11, libc/POSIX only). The AArch64
instruction interpreter, the guest address space and memory model, the ELF
loader, the rootfs path-containment resolver, the syscall layer, and the
signal/job-control delivery are written from scratch. The instruction-set,
FP/Advanced-SIMD, reciprocal-estimate, and cryptographic-extension (AES,
SHA-1/2/3/512, PMULL) implementations follow the pseudocode published in the
Arm Architecture Reference Manual; no third-party source code is included or
distributed with this project.

The instruction decode/execute core (lib/arm64, src/arm64chroot/core) is
shared with arm64emu.

qemu-aarch64 is used only as a differential-testing oracle (see
tests/arm64chroot) and as the reference for a handful of AArch64 ID-register
values chosen for guest compatibility; it is neither included nor linked.

chroot-ng (src/chroot-ng)
-------------------------

chroot-ng is an original implementation: a freestanding (no libc) AArch64
runtime that emulates a chroot environment and bind mounts in-process, using a
seccomp-BPF SIGSYS monitor and ahead-of-time rewriting of `svc #0` sites instead
of ptrace. The path-containment resolver, the userland ELF loader, the syscall
monitor and its dispatcher, the link2symlink layer, the AF_UNIX and NETLINK_ROUTE
emulation, and the freestanding runtime are written from scratch.

Portions are ported from arm64chroot — among them the guest-PID registry, the
synthesized /proc files, the System V shared memory / semaphore / message-queue
layer, the guest ptrace model, and the command-line help renderer.

chroot-ng is functionally comparable to proot but shares no code with it; no
third-party source code is included or distributed with this project. The UAPI
constants and signal-frame layouts in src/chroot-ng/include/cng/ are
re-declared from the stable AArch64 Linux syscall ABI rather than copied from
kernel headers, which is what keeps the freestanding build hermetic.

qemu-aarch64 is used only as a differential-testing oracle (see
tests/chroot-ng); it is neither included nor linked.
